Z||000000||Cheever2||11-27-2000||08:16 PM||||Man I love those faces on your sig line, but I don't know what they're from (should I?), and I can't see what the captions say. <BR> <BR>I searched for a previous post to attach this to, but didn't find an appropriate one.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||11-28-2000||10:42 PM||||The faces are "The Mighty Heroes," a spoof superhero cadre from the cartoon series of the same name. The adverntures of Strong Man, Rope Man, Diaper Man, Tornado Man, and Cuckoo Man were created in 1966 by Ralph Bakshi, of The Secret of NIMH and Cool World fame. Though they only lasted a year, they were rerun for years thereafter along with Mighty Mouse, the show that they had originally replaced. They were Bakshi's answer to the staid Justice League cartoons. In fact, all too often, the team simply got caught in Rope Man. Marvel Comics released a single comic book in 1988. Somehow, the theme song got stuck in my head, and I went on a crusade to find out what the music was from. I found it in a relatively simple search on Yahoo....<P>In not too long, thanks to my friends here, my site will come online, and I'll have something original in my sig line. Until then....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||6
